{"title":"Career roadmap · Network Planning Engineer","role":"Network Planning Engineer","summary":"A Network Planning Engineer designs, analyses, optimises and expands telecommunications networks. For an E&TC graduate, this is a directly relevant career because the degree provides foundations in communication systems, electronics, RF, signal processing, networking and transmission technologies.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Telecom/network planning trainee, RF/network engineer, transmission engineer, network operations roles"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"What should I specialise in?","output":"RAN planning, RF planning, transport/IP planning, fibre planning or network optimisation"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior planning engineer, optimisation specialist, network architect or technical lead"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How do I stay relevant?","output":"Telecom/network architect, planning manager, automation/AI-enabled network specialist or engineering leader"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical environments include mobile networks, optical fibre networks, IP networks, 5G/6G infrastructure, enterprise networks, data centres and telecom infrastructure providers."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","What to build","Skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Electronics + communication fundamentals"},{"text":"Circuit theory, digital electronics, signals, C/Python, mathematics"},{"text":"Simulate communication/electronic circuits"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Communication systems"},{"text":"Analog/digital communication, RF basics, antennas, transmission lines, probability"},{"text":"Build modulation/demodulation simulations"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Networking + telecom infrastructure"},{"t